(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m2"] = E["hr-m2"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-2-1"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-2-1-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-2-1","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Job descriptions","tr":"İş tanımları","fa":"شرح وظایف شغلی"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can turn a manager's notes into a job description, with essential and desirable requirements.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda bir yöneticinin notlarını zorunlu ve tercih edilen niteliklerle bir iş tanımına dönüştürebileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی یادداشت‌های یک مدیر را به شرح وظایف تبدیل کنی، با شرط‌های الزامی و شرط‌های ترجیحی."},"hook":{"en":"Sort every requirement into essential or desirable. The list decides who applies and who you choose. Omar said 'Class C, must have' and 'Arabic, nice'. Leyla turns that into two lists: essential and desirable.","tr":"Her şartı zorunlu ya da tercih edilen diye ayır. Bu liste kimin başvuracağını ve kimi seçeceğini belirler. Omar 'C sınıfı ehliyet şart' ve 'Arapça olsa iyi olur' dedi. Leyla bunu iki listeye çeviriyor: zorunlu ve tercih edilen.","fa":"هر شرط را الزامی یا ترجیحی مشخص کن. این فهرست تعیین می‌کند چه کسی درخواست بدهد و تو چه کسی را انتخاب کنی. عمر گفت «گواهینامه‌ی C واجب» و «عربی، خوب است». لیلا این را به دو فهرست تبدیل می‌کند: شرط‌های الزامی و ترجیحی."},"before":{"en":"Turn a manager’s notes into the requirements of a job ad: what is essential and what is desirable.","tr":"Bir yöneticinin notlarını iş ilanının şartlarına çevir: neyin zorunlu, neyin tercih sebebi olduğunu yaz.","fa":"یادداشت‌های یک مدیر را به شرایط آگهی شغلی تبدیل کن: چه چیزی ضروری است و چه چیزی امتیاز حساب می‌شود."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"5"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"4"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"Essential or desirable? Test each line","tr":"Zorunlu mu, tercih mi? Her satırı sına","fa":"الزامی یا ترجیحی؟ هر خط را امتحان کن"},"body":{"en":"Managers often mix needs and wishes. So test every requirement: could someone do this job without it? If not, it is essential. If yes, it is desirable. A false \"must\" can keep out good people.","tr":"Yöneticiler ihtiyaçla isteği sık sık karıştırır. Bu yüzden her şartı sına: biri bu işi o şart olmadan yapabilir mi? Yapamazsa şart zorunludur. Yapabilirse tercih edilen bir şarttır. Gereksiz bir zorunlu şart iyi adayları dışarıda bırakabilir.","fa":"مدیرها خیلی وقت‌ها نیاز و خواسته را با هم اشتباه می‌گیرند. پس هر شرط را امتحان کن: آیا کسی می‌تواند بدون آن این کار را انجام بدهد؟ اگر نه، الزامی است. اگر بله، ترجیحی است. شرط الزامی بی‌دلیل ممکن است آدم‌های خوب را کنار بگذارد."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Duties and requirements","tr":"Görevler ve gereksinimler","fa":"وظایف و شرایط احراز"},"steps":[{"en":"Duties: present simple, or You will + verb.","tr":"Görevler: present simple ya da You will + fiil.","fa":"وظایف را با حال ساده یا با You will و فعل ساده بنویس.","ex":"The driver checks the load before each trip."},{"en":"Essential: must + bare verb, or is required.","tr":"Zorunlu: must + yalın fiil ya da is required.","fa":"شرط الزامی را با must و فعل ساده یا با is required بنویس.","ex":"Candidates must hold a Class C licence."},{"en":"Desirable: would be an advantage, or is preferred.","tr":"Tercih edilen: would be an advantage ya da is preferred.","fa":"شرط ترجیحی را با would be an advantage یا is preferred بنویس.","ex":"Cold-chain experience would be an advantage."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Type","Pattern"],"tr":["Tür","Kalıp"],"fa":["نوع جمله","الگو"]},"rows":[["Duty","The driver delivers... / You will be responsible for..."],["Essential","must + base verb / are required to + base verb"],["Desirable","would be an advantage / is preferred / ideally"],["Not allowed","must not (never \"must to\")"]]},"tip":{"en":"Turkish 'sahip olmalıdır' and Persian 'bayad dashte bashad' sound like must + to have, so learners write 'must to hold'. English must takes the bare verb, with no to.","tr":"'Adaylar C sınıfı ehliyete sahip olmalıdır' cümlesini çevirirken 'must to hold' yazılabiliyor. İngilizcede must'tan sonra to gelmez: Candidates must hold...","fa":"در فارسی «باید داشته باشد» می‌گوییم و فارسی‌زبان‌ها گاهی «must to hold» می‌نویسند. در انگلیسی بعد از must هیچ‌وقت to نمی‌آید: «⁨Candidates must hold...⁩»"},"wrong":"Candidates must to hold a Class C licence.","right":"Candidates must hold a Class C licence."},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"Is that essential or desirable?","meaning":{"en":"Separates must-haves from nice-to-haves.","tr":"Olmazsa olmazı tercihten ayırır.","fa":"شرط‌های الزامی را از شرط‌های ترجیحی جدا می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"What does a typical day look like?","meaning":{"en":"Asks for concrete duties.","tr":"Somut görevleri sorar.","fa":"وظایف واقعی و روزمره را می‌پرسد."}},{"phrase":"Could you give me an example?","meaning":{"en":"Turns a vague word into a real task.","tr":"Belirsiz sözü gerçek bir göreve çevirir.","fa":"یک کلمه‌ی کلی را به یک کار واقعی تبدیل می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"requirement","meaning":{"en":"Something that is needed.","tr":"gereksinim.","fa":"شرط؛ الزام"}},{"phrase":"shift","meaning":{"en":"A fixed period of work time.","tr":"vardiya.","fa":"شیفت؛ نوبت کاری"}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"Essential must be truly essential","tr":"Zorunlu, gerçekten zorunlu olmalı","fa":"شرط الزامی باید واقعاً الزامی باشد"},"body":{"en":"In the UK, the US and the EU, \"essential\" requirements must be genuinely needed to do the job, because they can later be questioned as unfair. Asking a manager \"is that really essential?\" is part of an HR specialist's job.","tr":"Birleşik Krallık, ABD ve AB'de \"zorunlu\" gereksinimler işin yapılması için gerçekten gerekli olmalıdır; aksi hâlde sonradan adil olmadığı için sorgulanabilir. Bir yöneticiye \"Bu gerçekten zorunlu mu?\" diye sormak İK uzmanının işidir.","fa":"در بریتانیا، آمریکا و اتحادیه‌ی اروپا، شرطی که «الزامی» اعلام می‌شود باید واقعاً برای انجام کار لازم باشد، چون ممکن است بعدها به‌عنوان شرطی تبعیض‌آمیز زیر سؤال برود. اینکه از مدیر بپرسی «این شرط واقعاً الزامی است؟» بخشی از کار کارشناس منابع انسانی است."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از فهرست آرزوها تا دو فهرست روشن"},"text":"Facts: The job needs a Class C licence. Spoken Arabic helps, but the job can be done without it.","item":"Must have a licence, Arabic and a great personality.","why":{"en":"Weak: a wish list, and every line sounds like a must. Strong: two lists, one for each kind of line.","tr":"Zayıf: bir istek listesi; her satır zorunlu gibi. Güçlü: iki liste, her biri kendi türünde.","fa":"نسخه‌ی اول فهرستی از آرزوهاست و انگار همه‌چیز الزامی است. نسخه‌ی دوم دو فهرست دارد، هر کدام برای یک نوع شرط."},"answer":"Essential: a valid Class C licence. Desirable: spoken Arabic.","cut":["and a great personality"],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap what no one can check in an interview.","tr":"Bir görüşmede kimsenin kontrol edemeyeceği şeye dokun.","fa":"روی چیزی بزن که هیچ‌کس نمی‌تواند در مصاحبه بسنجدش."}},"quick":{"prompt":"A manager wants \"must be under 35\" in the essentials. What do you do?","options":["Ask: is that really essential to do the job?","Add it: the manager decides","Move it to desirable"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Ask whether it is really essential: an essential requirement must be needed to do the job, and an age limit can be questioned as unfair.","tr":"Bunun gerçekten zorunlu olup olmadığını sor: Zorunlu bir şart işi yapmak için gerçekten gerekli olmalı; yaş sınırı haksız diye sorgulanabilir.","fa":"بپرس که واقعاً ضروری است یا نه: شرط ضروری باید واقعاً برای انجام کار لازم باشد و محدودیت سنی ممکن است ناعادلانه شمرده شود."},"point":4},"remember":{"en":"Could the person do the job without it? No: essential, use must. Yes: desirable, use would be an advantage. Result of this lesson: you can sort a manager's notes into essential and desirable. You also have a job description.","tr":"Kişi bu olmadan işi yapabilir mi? Hayır: zorunlu, must kullan. Evet: tercih edilen, would be an advantage kullan. Bu dersin sonucu: bir yöneticinin notlarını zorunlu ve tercih edilen olarak ayırabilirsin ve elinde bir iş tanımı olur.","fa":"آیا آن فرد بدون این شرط می‌تواند کار را انجام دهد؟ نه: الزامی است، must بنویس. بله: ترجیحی است، would be an advantage بنویس. حالا می‌توانی یادداشت‌های مدیر را به شرط الزامی و ترجیحی تقسیم کنی. یک شرح وظایف هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"Participle clauses in job descriptions","tr":"İş tanımlarında ortaç yapıları (participle clauses)","fa":"عبارت‌های وصفیِ فعلی در شرح وظایف"},"steps":[{"en":"-ing clause = who + verb, shorter.","tr":"-ing yapısı = who + fiil, daha kısa.","fa":"عبارت -ing همان who و فعل است، فقط کوتاه‌تر.","ex":"a team of 20 drivers working across the UAE"},{"en":"An opening -ing clause describes the subject that follows.","tr":"Baştaki -ing yapısı ardından gelen özneyi anlatır.","fa":"عبارت ⁨-ing⁩ در ابتدای جمله، فاعلِ بعد از خودش را توصیف می‌کند.","ex":"Reporting to Omar, you will plan routes."},{"en":"The person does it: -ing, not the past participle.","tr":"Eylemi kişi yapıyorsa: -ing, past participle değil.","fa":"اگر خود شخص کار را انجام می‌دهد، -ing بیاور، نه اسم مفعول.","ex":"Reporting to..., not Reported to..."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Long form","Participle clause"],"tr":["Uzun biçim","Ortaç yapısı"],"fa":["شکل کامل","عبارت وصفی (participle clause)"]},"rows":[["You will report to the Operations Manager. You will plan routes.","Reporting to the Operations Manager, you will plan routes."],["a team of drivers who work across the UAE","a team of drivers working across the UAE"],["You will work closely with the warehouse. You will...","Working closely with the warehouse, you will..."]]},"body":{"en":"B2 track: your job description must open with a participle clause (\"Reporting to...\") and use one more -ing clause.","tr":"B2 yolu: iş tanımın bir ortaç yapısıyla (\"Reporting to...\") başlamalı ve bir -ing yapısı daha içermeli.","fa":"مسیر ⁨B2⁩: شرح وظایف تو باید با یک عبارت وصفی شروع شود («⁨Reporting to...⁩») و یک عبارت ⁨-ing⁩ دیگر هم داشته باشد."}},"source":{"en":"Based on Acas guidance on advertising a job.","tr":"Acas’ın iş ilanı verme rehberine dayanır.","fa":"بر پایه‌ی راهنمای Acas درباره‌ی آگهی استخدام."}},"grammar":{"id":"c-hr-2-1-g","level":"B1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-2-1","title":"Duties and requirements","titleTr":"Görevler ve gereksinimler","exp":{"en":"A job description has two kinds of sentences. Duties say what the person does, in the present simple: \"The driver delivers goods and checks the load.\" or with will: \"You will be responsible for...\". Requirements say what the person needs. Essential means the person cannot do the job without it: \"Candidates must hold a Class C licence.\" (must + base verb, no \"to\"; or \"are required to hold\"). Desirable means it helps but is not necessary: \"Experience in cold-chain transport would be an advantage.\" Keep the two lists apart so applicants know where they stand, and so your shortlist is fair.","tr":"İş tanımında iki tür cümle vardır. Görevler kişinin ne yaptığını present simple ile söyler: \"The driver delivers goods and checks the load.\" ya da will ile: \"You will be responsible for...\". Gereksinimler kişinin neye ihtiyacı olduğunu söyler. Zorunlu (essential), o olmadan işin yapılamayacağı demektir: \"Candidates must hold a Class C licence.\" (must + yalın fiil, \"to\" yok; ya da \"are required to hold\"). Tercih edilen (desirable), yardımcı olur ama şart değildir: \"Experience in cold-chain transport would be an advantage.\" İki listeyi ayrı tut; böylece adaylar nerede durduklarını bilir ve kısa listen adil olur.","fa":"شرح وظایف (job description) دو نوع جمله دارد. جمله‌های «وظایف» (duties) می‌گویند این فرد چه کار می‌کند؛ با حال ساده: «⁨The driver delivers goods and checks the load.⁩» یا با will: «⁨You will be responsible for...⁩». جمله‌های «شرایط» (requirements) می‌گویند این فرد چه چیزهایی باید داشته باشد. شرط الزامی (essential) یعنی بدون آن نمی‌شود این کار را انجام داد: «⁨Candidates must hold a Class C licence.⁩» (بعد از must فعل ساده و بدون to می‌آید؛ یا بگو «are required to hold»). شرط ترجیحی (desirable) همان چیزی است که در آگهی‌های فارسی با «... امتیاز محسوب می‌شود» می‌نویسیم: «⁨Experience in cold-chain transport would be an advantage.⁩» این دو فهرست را از هم جدا نگه دار تا متقاضیان بدانند کجای کار ایستاده‌اند و فهرست منتخب تو هم منصفانه باشد."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Type","Pattern"],"tr":["Tür","Kalıp"],"fa":["نوع جمله","الگو"]},"rows":[["Duty","The driver delivers... / You will be responsible for..."],["Essential","must + base verb / are required to + base verb"],["Desirable","would be an advantage / is preferred / ideally"],["Not allowed","must not (never \"must to\")"]]},"wrong":"Candidates must to hold a Class C licence.","right":"Candidates must hold a Class C licence.","blank":{"sentence":"Candidates ___ hold a valid Class C licence.","word":"must","distractors":["must to","are"]},"wrong2":"Experience in cold-chain transport is advantage.","right2":"Experience in cold-chain transport would be an advantage.","blank2":{"sentence":"Experience in cold-chain transport ___ an advantage.","word":"would be","distractors":["would","is being"]},"expParts":{"tryFrom":"blank","hook":{"en":"Omar said 'Class C, must have' and 'Arabic, nice'. Leyla turns that into two lists: essential and desirable.","tr":"Omar 'C sınıfı ehliyet şart' ve 'Arapça olsa iyi olur' dedi. Leyla bunu iki listeye çeviriyor: zorunlu ve tercih edilen.","fa":"عمر گفت «گواهینامه‌ی C واجب» و «عربی، خوب است». لیلا این را به دو فهرست تبدیل می‌کند: شرط‌های الزامی و ترجیحی."},"tryWhy":{"en":"must: must is followed by the bare verb. 'must to' is never correct.","tr":"must: must'tan sonra yalın fiil gelir. 'must to' hiçbir zaman doğru değildir.","fa":"جواب must است: بعد از must فعل ساده می‌آید. must to هیچ‌وقت درست نیست."},"rule":[{"en":"Duties: present simple, or You will + verb.","tr":"Görevler: present simple ya da You will + fiil.","fa":"وظایف را با حال ساده یا با You will و فعل ساده بنویس.","ex":"The driver checks the load before each trip."},{"en":"Essential: must + bare verb, or is required.","tr":"Zorunlu: must + yalın fiil ya da is required.","fa":"شرط الزامی را با must و فعل ساده یا با is required بنویس.","ex":"Candidates must hold a Class C licence."},{"en":"Desirable: would be an advantage, or is preferred.","tr":"Tercih edilen: would be an advantage ya da is preferred.","fa":"شرط ترجیحی را با would be an advantage یا is preferred بنویس.","ex":"Cold-chain experience would be an advantage."}],"test":{"en":"Could the person do the job without it? No: essential, use must. Yes: desirable, use would be an advantage.","tr":"Kişi bu olmadan işi yapabilir mi? Hayır: zorunlu, must kullan. Evet: tercih edilen, would be an advantage kullan.","fa":"آیا آن فرد بدون این شرط می‌تواند کار را انجام دهد؟ نه: الزامی است، must بنویس. بله: ترجیحی است، would be an advantage بنویس."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish 'sahip olmalıdır' and Persian 'bayad dashte bashad' sound like must + to have, so learners write 'must to hold'. English must takes the bare verb, with no to.","tr":"'Adaylar C sınıfı ehliyete sahip olmalıdır' cümlesini çevirirken 'must to hold' yazılabiliyor. İngilizcede must'tan sonra to gelmez: Candidates must hold...","fa":"در فارسی «باید داشته باشد» می‌گوییم و فارسی‌زبان‌ها گاهی «must to hold» می‌نویسند. در انگلیسی بعد از must هیچ‌وقت to نمی‌آید: «⁨Candidates must hold...⁩»"}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["must to","must to have","should to"],"fix":{"en":"must takes the bare verb: 'Candidates must hold a Class C licence.'","tr":"must yalın fiil alır: 'Candidates must hold a Class C licence.'","fa":"بعد از must فعل ساده می‌آید: «⁨Candidates must hold a Class C licence.⁩»"}},{"find":["is advantage","is a advantage"],"fix":{"en":"Say 'would be an advantage' for desirable points, and turn vague words into a duty: 'You will speak with customers politely.'","tr":"Tercih edilen şartlar için 'would be an advantage' de; belirsiz sözleri bir göreve çevir: 'You will speak with customers politely.'","fa":"برای شرط‌های ترجیحی بنویس «would be an advantage» و عبارت‌های مبهم را به یک وظیفه‌ی مشخص تبدیل کن: «⁨You will speak with customers politely.⁩»"}}]},"b2":{"id":"c-hr-2-1-b2","level":"B2","track":"B2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-2-1","title":"Participle clauses in job descriptions","titleTr":"İş tanımlarında ortaç yapıları (participle clauses)","exp":{"en":"Professional job descriptions pack information into short -ing clauses: \"Reporting to the Operations Manager, you will plan daily routes.\", \"You will join a team of 20 drivers working across the UAE.\" The -ing clause replaces \"who reports\" or \"who work\", so the text is shorter and sounds more expert. Two rules. The -ing form must describe the subject of the main clause: in \"Reporting to Omar, you will...\" it is you who reports. And use -ing (active), not the past participle, when the person does the action: \"Reporting to...\", not \"Reported to...\".","tr":"Profesyonel iş tanımları bilgiyi kısa -ing yapılarına sığdırır: \"Reporting to the Operations Manager, you will plan daily routes.\", \"You will join a team of 20 drivers working across the UAE.\" -ing yapısı \"who reports\" ya da \"who work\" yerine geçer; metin kısalır ve daha uzman bir dil gibi durur. Türkçedeki \"-en/-an\" sıfat-fiillerine (\"Operasyon Müdürüne bağlı çalışan\") benzer. İki kural var. -ing biçimi ana cümlenin öznesini anlatmalıdır: \"Reporting to Omar, you will...\" cümlesinde rapor veren kişi you'dur. Eylemi kişi yapıyorsa past participle değil -ing (etken) kullan: \"Reporting to...\"; \"Reported to...\" değil.","fa":"شرح وظایف حرفه‌ای اطلاعات را در عبارت‌های کوتاهِ ⁨-ing⁩ فشرده می‌کند: «⁨Reporting to the Operations Manager, you will plan daily routes.⁩» و «⁨You will join a team of 20 drivers working across the UAE.⁩» عبارت ⁨-ing⁩ جای «⁨who reports⁩» یا «⁨who work⁩» را می‌گیرد؛ متن کوتاه‌تر می‌شود و حرفه‌ای‌تر به نظر می‌رسد. دو قاعده را رعایت کن. اول: عبارت ⁨-ing⁩ باید درباره‌ی فاعل جمله‌ی اصلی باشد؛ در «⁨Reporting to Omar, you will...⁩» کسی که به عمر گزارش می‌دهد همان ⁨you⁩ است. دوم: وقتی خودِ فرد کار را انجام می‌دهد، شکل ⁨-ing⁩ (معلوم) را بیاور، نه اسم مفعول را: «⁨Reporting to...⁩»، نه «⁨Reported to...⁩»."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Long form","Participle clause"],"tr":["Uzun biçim","Ortaç yapısı"],"fa":["شکل کامل","عبارت وصفی (participle clause)"]},"rows":[["You will report to the Operations Manager. You will plan routes.","Reporting to the Operations Manager, you will plan routes."],["a team of drivers who work across the UAE","a team of drivers working across the UAE"],["You will work closely with the warehouse. You will...","Working closely with the warehouse, you will..."]]},"wrong":"Reported to the Operations Manager, you will plan daily routes.","right":"Reporting to the Operations Manager, you will plan daily routes.","blank":{"sentence":"___ to the Operations Manager, you will plan daily routes.","word":"Reporting","distractors":["Report","Reported"]},"wrong2":"You will join a team of 20 drivers works across the UAE.","right2":"You will join a team of 20 drivers working across the UAE.","blank2":{"sentence":"You will join a team of 20 drivers ___ across the UAE.","word":"working","distractors":["works","work"]},"useIn":{"en":"B2 track: your job description must open with a participle clause (\"Reporting to...\") and use one more -ing clause.","tr":"B2 yolu: iş tanımın bir ortaç yapısıyla (\"Reporting to...\") başlamalı ve bir -ing yapısı daha içermeli.","fa":"مسیر ⁨B2⁩: شرح وظایف تو باید با یک عبارت وصفی شروع شود («⁨Reporting to...⁩») و یک عبارت ⁨-ing⁩ دیگر هم داشته باشد."},"exitItem":{"from":"hr-2-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"___ in our Dubai depot, the role includes some weekend work.","options":["Basing","Based","Base"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Based: the role receives the action (it is based in Dubai), so a past participle opens the clause. 'Basing' would mean the role bases something, and 'Base' is a verb or noun.","tr":"Based: görev eylemi alır (Dubai'de konumlanır), bu yüzden yan cümle üçüncü hâlle başlar. 'Basing' görevin bir şeyi konumlandırdığı anlamına gelir; 'Base' fiil ya da isimdir.","fa":"Based درست است، چون این سمت در دبی مستقر است و برای همین اسم مفعول می‌آید. basing یعنی خود سمت چیزی را مستقر می‌کند و base فعل یا اسم است."}},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"Real job ads say a lot in few words: 'Reporting to the Operations Manager, you will...'","tr":"Gerçek iş ilanları az sözle çok şey söyler: 'Reporting to the Operations Manager, you will...'","fa":"آگهی‌های حرفه‌ای با کلمه‌های کم حرف زیادی می‌زنند: «⁨Reporting to the Operations Manager, you will...⁩»"},"tryWhy":{"en":"working: the -ing clause replaces 'who work'. The drivers do the action, so it is active.","tr":"working: -ing yapısı 'who work' yerine geçer. Eylemi sürücüler yapıyor, bu yüzden etken.","fa":"جواب working است: عبارت -ing جای who work را می‌گیرد. کار را خود راننده‌ها انجام می‌دهند، پس معلوم است."},"rule":[{"en":"-ing clause = who + verb, shorter.","tr":"-ing yapısı = who + fiil, daha kısa.","fa":"عبارت -ing همان who و فعل است، فقط کوتاه‌تر.","ex":"a team of 20 drivers working across the UAE"},{"en":"An opening -ing clause describes the subject that follows.","tr":"Baştaki -ing yapısı ardından gelen özneyi anlatır.","fa":"عبارت ⁨-ing⁩ در ابتدای جمله، فاعلِ بعد از خودش را توصیف می‌کند.","ex":"Reporting to Omar, you will plan routes."},{"en":"The person does it: -ing, not the past participle.","tr":"Eylemi kişi yapıyorsa: -ing, past participle değil.","fa":"اگر خود شخص کار را انجام می‌دهد، -ing بیاور، نه اسم مفعول.","ex":"Reporting to..., not Reported to..."}],"test":{"en":"Put 'who' in front: 'who reports to Omar' works? Then the -ing form is right.","tr":"Başına 'who' koy: 'who reports to Omar' oluyor mu? O zaman -ing doğru.","fa":"اولش ⁨who⁩ بگذار: «⁨who reports to Omar⁩» درست درمی‌آید؟ پس شکل ⁨-ing⁩ درست است."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish packs this into -an/-en ('BAE genelinde çalışan sürücüler') and Persian into a 'ke' clause. English uses -ing after the noun, with no who and no extra verb.","tr":"Türkçede bu bilgi '-an/-en' ile verilir: 'BAE genelinde çalışan 20 sürücü'. İngilizcede -ing ismin arkasına gelir: 20 drivers working across the UAE.","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «۲۰ راننده که در سراسر امارات کار می‌کنند». انگلیسی می‌تواند «که» و فعل را حذف کند و ⁨-ing⁩ را بعد از اسم بگذارد: «⁨20 drivers working across the UAE⁩»."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["reported to the","reported to omar"],"fix":{"en":"If the person reports, use -ing: 'Reporting to the Operations Manager, you will...'","tr":"Kişi rapor veriyorsa -ing kullan: 'Reporting to the Operations Manager, you will...'","fa":"اگر خود شخص گزارش می‌دهد، ⁨-ing⁩ بیاور: «⁨Reporting to the Operations Manager, you will...⁩»"}},{"find":["drivers works","people works","drivers who working","team who working"],"fix":{"en":"After a plural noun use -ing (drivers working) or who + verb (drivers who work).","tr":"Çoğul isimden sonra -ing (drivers working) ya da who + fiil (drivers who work) kullan.","fa":"بعد از اسم جمع یا -ing بیاور (drivers working) یا who و فعل (drivers who work)."}}]},"vocab":{"id":"c-hr-2-1-v","level":"B1","category":"vocab","course":"hr","unit":"hr-2-1","goals":["career"],"title":{"en":"Job Description Words","tr":"İş Tanımı Kelimeleri","fa":"واژه‌های شرح وظایف"},"cards":[{"word":"job description","sentence":"The job description lists the main duties.","meaning":{"en":"A document that explains what a job involves.","tr":"iş tanımı.","fa":"شرح شغل؛ شرح وظایف (سندی که می‌گوید یک شغل شامل چه کارهایی است)"}},{"word":"person specification","sentence":"The person specification says which skills are essential.","meaning":{"en":"A list of skills and experience the ideal person has.","tr":"aday profili.","fa":"شرایط احراز شغل؛ ویژگی‌ها و سوابقی که فرد ایدئال دارد"}},{"word":"duties","sentence":"His main duties are delivery and loading.","meaning":{"en":"The tasks that are part of a job.","tr":"görevler.","fa":"وظایف"}},{"word":"essential","sentence":"A Class C licence is essential for this role.","meaning":{"en":"Absolutely necessary.","tr":"zorunlu.","fa":"الزامی؛ ضروری"}},{"word":"desirable","sentence":"Arabic is desirable but not essential.","meaning":{"en":"Useful but not necessary.","tr":"tercih edilen.","fa":"ترجیحی؛ امتیاز محسوب می‌شود"}},{"word":"qualification","sentence":"The role needs no university qualification.","meaning":{"en":"A certificate or degree from training.","tr":"nitelik, diploma.","fa":"مدرک (تحصیلی یا حرفه‌ای)"}},{"word":"requirement","sentence":"Each requirement must be clear and fair.","meaning":{"en":"Something that is needed.","tr":"gereksinim.","fa":"شرط؛ الزام"}},{"word":"shift","sentence":"The driver works a night shift twice a week.","meaning":{"en":"A fixed period of work time.","tr":"vardiya.","fa":"شیفت؛ نوبت کاری"}},{"word":"salary range","sentence":"The salary range is 7,000 to 9,000 dirhams.","meaning":{"en":"The lowest and highest pay for a job.","tr":"maaş aralığı.","fa":"بازه‌ی حقوق (کمترین و بیشترین حقوق برای یک شغل)"}},{"word":"vacancy","sentence":"We have three vacancies in Dubai.","gap":"vacancies","accept":["vacancies","vacancy"],"meaning":{"en":"A job that is open and needs someone.","tr":"açık pozisyon.","fa":"موقعیت شغلی خالی؛ فرصت شغلی"}}]},"story":{"id":"c-hr-2-1-s","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","course":"hr","unit":"hr-2-1","title":{"en":"Omar's Notes","tr":"Omar'ın Notları","fa":"یادداشت‌های عمر"},"text":"Omar sent his notes as a voice message, in the middle of a loading bay. Leyla could hear trucks and a lot of shouting.\n\n\"Three drivers. Good with people. Not afraid of long days. Class C, must have. Arabic, nice, but English is more important. Night shifts sometimes. Cold-chain, big plus. Salary, I don't know, ask finance.\"\n\nLeyla opened a blank page and typed three headings: Duties, Essential, Desirable.\n\nUnder Duties she wrote: The driver delivers goods to customers in Dubai and Sharjah. The driver checks the load before each trip. You will be responsible for the vehicle's daily log.\n\nUnder Essential: Candidates must hold a valid Class C licence. Candidates must be able to work night shifts. Good spoken English is required.\n\nUnder Desirable: Experience in cold-chain transport would be an advantage. Arabic is preferred.\n\nShe stopped at \"Good with people.\" What did that mean on a page? She changed it to: You will speak with customers politely, even when a delivery is late.\n\nOmar read the draft on his break. \"Where is the salary?\" \"You said ask finance.\" \"Fine. Seven to nine thousand dirhams.\" She added the line. Then she did something she had not planned. She sent the page to Hasan, one of Atlas's best Istanbul drivers, and asked: would you apply for this?\n\nHis answer came back in three minutes: \"Where does it say what a normal day looks like?\"","vocab":[{"word":"loading bay","en":"The area where trucks are loaded.","tr":"yükleme rampası","fa":"سکوی بارگیری"},{"word":"heading","en":"A short title above a list.","tr":"başlık","fa":"عنوان؛ تیتر بالای یک فهرست"},{"word":"daily log","en":"A record of what happens each day.","tr":"günlük kayıt","fa":"گزارش روزانه؛ دفتر ثبت روزانه"},{"word":"draft","en":"A first version of a text.","tr":"taslak","fa":"پیش‌نویس"},{"word":"break","en":"A short rest from work.","tr":"mola","fa":"استراحت کوتاه بین کار"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"Why did Leyla make three headings?","options":["To separate duties from essential and desirable requirements","To make the page look long","Because Omar asked her to"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"Choose the correct sentence.","options":["Candidates must to hold a licence.","Candidates must hold a licence.","Candidates must holding a licence."],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Why did Leyla change \"Good with people\"?","options":["It was too vague for a written page","It was rude","It was too long"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"What does Hasan probably feel about the draft?","options":["Interested, but unsure what the day is really like","Angry about the salary","Sure he will not apply"],"correct":0}],"notice":{"en":"Omar's voice note mixes must-haves and nice-to-haves. As you read, sort them: which ones go under Essential?","tr":"Omar'ın sesli notunda şartlar ve 'olsa iyi olur'lar karışık. Okurken ayır: hangileri Zorunlu başlığına girer?","fa":"پیام صوتی عمر شرط‌های واجب و «خوب است باشد»ها را با هم مخلوط کرده است. موقع خواندن جدایشان کن: کدام‌ها زیر «الزامی» می‌روند؟"},"bridge":{"en":"Leyla's three headings used three sentence patterns. Next: see how they work.","tr":"Leyla'nın üç başlığı üç farklı cümle kalıbı kullandı. Sırada: nasıl çalıştıklarını gör.","fa":"سه عنوان لیلا سه الگوی جمله داشتند. قدم بعد: ببین چطور کار می‌کنند."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-2-1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-2-1","topic":{"en":"Clarifying a Vacancy with a Manager","tr":"Bir Yöneticiyle Açık Pozisyonu Netleştirmek","fa":"پرسیدن جزئیات یک موقعیت شغلی از مدیر"},"warmup":{"en":"Think of the last job you or a friend applied for. What was unclear in the advert?","tr":"Sen ya da bir arkadaşının son başvurduğu işi düşün. İlanda neresi belirsizdi?","fa":"آخرین آگهی شغلی‌ای را به یاد بیاور که خودت یا یکی از دوستانت برایش درخواست داد. چه چیزی در آن آگهی روشن نبود؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Ask the manager what the main duties are.","tr":"Yöneticiye ana görevlerin neler olduğunu sor.","fa":"از مدیر بپرس وظایف اصلی این شغل چیست."},{"en":"Ask which requirements are essential and which are only desirable.","tr":"Hangi gereksinimlerin zorunlu, hangilerinin sadece tercih edilen olduğunu sor.","fa":"بپرس کدام شرایط الزامی است و کدام فقط ترجیحی."},{"en":"Ask about shifts, salary range and start date.","tr":"Vardiya, maaş aralığı ve başlangıç tarihini sor.","fa":"درباره‌ی شیفت‌ها، بازه‌ی حقوق و تاریخ شروع کار بپرس."}],"followups":[{"en":"The manager says: \"Good with people.\" Ask a follow-up to turn it into a concrete duty.","tr":"Yönetici \"Good with people\" diyor. Bunu somut bir göreve çevirecek bir takip sorusu sor.","fa":"مدیر می‌گوید: «⁨Good with people.⁩» با یک سؤال تکمیلی، این جمله‌ی کلی را به یک وظیفه‌ی مشخص تبدیل کن."},{"en":"Now describe one real job at your company: two duties and one true requirement.","tr":"Şimdi şirketindeki gerçek bir işi anlat: iki görev ve bir gerçek şart.","fa":"حالا یک شغل واقعی در شرکتت را توصیف کن: دو وظیفه و یک شرط واقعی."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"Is that essential or desirable?","meaning":{"en":"Separates must-haves from nice-to-haves.","tr":"Olmazsa olmazı tercihten ayırır.","fa":"شرط‌های الزامی را از شرط‌های ترجیحی جدا می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"What does a typical day look like?","meaning":{"en":"Asks for concrete duties.","tr":"Somut görevleri sorar.","fa":"وظایف واقعی و روزمره را می‌پرسد."}},{"phrase":"Could you give me an example?","meaning":{"en":"Turns a vague word into a real task.","tr":"Belirsiz sözü gerçek bir göreve çevirir.","fa":"یک کلمه‌ی کلی را به یک کار واقعی تبدیل می‌کند."}}],"culture":{"en":"In the UK, the US and the EU, \"essential\" requirements must be genuinely needed to do the job, because they can later be questioned as unfair. Asking a manager \"is that really essential?\" is part of an HR specialist's job.","tr":"Birleşik Krallık, ABD ve AB'de \"zorunlu\" gereksinimler işin yapılması için gerçekten gerekli olmalıdır; aksi hâlde sonradan adil olmadığı için sorgulanabilir. Bir yöneticiye \"Bu gerçekten zorunlu mu?\" diye sormak İK uzmanının işidir.","fa":"در بریتانیا، آمریکا و اتحادیه‌ی اروپا، شرطی که «الزامی» اعلام می‌شود باید واقعاً برای انجام کار لازم باشد، چون ممکن است بعدها به‌عنوان شرطی تبعیض‌آمیز زیر سؤال برود. اینکه از مدیر بپرسی «این شرط واقعاً الزامی است؟» بخشی از کار کارشناس منابع انسانی است."},"model":"Thanks for the notes, Omar. I have a few questions. What does a typical day look like for the drivers? You said Class C licence. Is that essential or desirable? And Arabic, is that essential, or would it just be an advantage? You also said good with people. Could you give me an example? Finally, what is the salary range and the start date?","selfCheck":[{"en":"I asked about the main duties or a typical day.","tr":"Ana görevleri ya da tipik bir günü sordum.","fa":"درباره‌ی وظایف اصلی یا یک روز معمولی پرسیدم."},{"en":"I asked 'Is that essential or desirable?'","tr":"'Is that essential or desirable?' diye sordum.","fa":"پرسیدم «⁨Is that essential or desirable?⁩»"},{"en":"I turned 'good with people' into a concrete question.","tr":"'Good with people' ifadesini somut bir soruya çevirdim.","fa":"«good with people» را به یک سؤال مشخص تبدیل کردم."},{"en":"I asked about shifts, salary or the start date.","tr":"Vardiyaları, maaşı ya da başlangıç tarihini sordum.","fa":"درباره‌ی شیفت، حقوق یا تاریخ شروع پرسیدم."}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-2-1-w","title":{"en":"A job description from Omar's notes","tr":"Omar'ın notlarından iş tanımı","fa":"شرح وظایف از روی یادداشت‌های عمر"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-2-1","type":"writing","difficulty":"medium","prompt":{"en":"Turn Omar's notes into a job description for \"Delivery Driver, Dubai\": who the driver reports to, 2 duties, 3 essential and 2 desirable requirements, plus shift and salary.","tr":"Omar'ın notlarını \"Delivery Driver, Dubai\" için bir iş tanımına çevir: sürücünün kime bağlı çalışacağı, 2 görev, 3 zorunlu ve 2 tercih edilen gereksinim, ayrıca vardiya ve maaş.","fa":"یادداشت‌های عمر را به شرح وظایف شغل «Delivery Driver, Dubai» تبدیل کن: راننده زیر نظر چه کسی کار می‌کند، دو وظیفه، سه شرط الزامی و دو شرط ترجیحی، به‌علاوه‌ی شیفت و حقوق."},"model":"Delivery Driver, Dubai. Reports to: Operations Manager, Dubai. Location: Dubai depot. Duties: The driver delivers goods to customers in Dubai and Sharjah. You will be responsible for the vehicle's daily log. Essential: Candidates must hold a valid Class C licence. Candidates must be able to work night shifts. Good spoken English is required. Desirable: Experience in cold-chain transport would be an advantage. Arabic is preferred. Shift: some nights. Salary: 7,000-9,000 dirhams.","frame":"Delivery Driver, Dubai. Reports to: ___. Location: ___. Duties: The driver ___. You will be responsible for ___. Essential: Candidates must ___. Candidates must be able to ___. ___ is required. Desirable: ___ would be an advantage. ___ is preferred. Shift: ___. Salary: ___.","words":[{"word":"essential"},{"word":"desirable"},{"word":"responsible for"}],"minWords":55,"minSentences":6,"rubric":["Task done: reports to, duties, essential, desirable, shift, salary","Organised: four labelled sections","Language: present simple for duties; must + base verb; would be an advantage","Tone: neutral, specific, no vague words like \"good with people\""],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: bağlı olunan yönetici, görevler, zorunlu şartlar, tercih edilen şartlar, vardiya, maaş","Düzen: dört başlık altında","Dil: görevler için present simple; must + yalın fiil; would be an advantage","Üslup: tarafsız, somut; \"good with people\" gibi belirsiz sözler yok"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: مدیر مستقیم، وظایف، شرط‌های الزامی، شرط‌های ترجیحی، شیفت، حقوق","نظم: چهار بخش با عنوان","زبان: حال ساده برای وظایف؛ must با شکل ساده‌ی فعل؛ would be an advantage","لحن: بی‌طرف و مشخص؛ بدون عبارت‌های مبهمی مثل «good with people»"]},"portfolio":null,"parts":[{"t":{"en":"Who the job reports to","tr":"Kime bağlı çalışacağı","fa":"اینکه زیر نظر چه کسی کار می‌کند"},"find":["reports to","report to","line manager"],"sample":"Operations Manager, Dubai"},{"t":{"en":"Two duties","tr":"İki görev","fa":"دو وظیفه"},"find":["delivers","responsible for","duties","you will"],"sample":"deliver goods in Dubai and Sharjah; keep the daily vehicle log"},{"t":{"en":"The essential requirements","tr":"Zorunlu şartlar","fa":"شرایط ضروری"},"find":["essential","must","required"],"sample":"Class C licence; night shifts; good spoken English"},{"t":{"en":"The desirable requirements","tr":"Tercih sebebi olan şartlar","fa":"شرایطی که امتیاز حساب می‌شوند"},"find":["desirable","would be an advantage","preferred"],"sample":"cold-chain experience; Arabic"},{"t":{"en":"Shift and salary","tr":"Vardiya ve maaş","fa":"شیفت و حقوق"},"find":["shift","salary","dirhams"],"sample":"some nights; 7,000-9,000 dirhams"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-2-1-p","title":{"en":"Hasan reads the draft","tr":"Hasan taslağı okuyor","fa":"حسن پیش‌نویس را می‌خواند"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-2-1","type":"perspective","minSentences":2,"prompt":{"en":"You are Hasan, a driver reading the draft. Write 2-3 sentences in first person: what is missing, and what would make you apply?","tr":"Taslağı okuyan bir şoför olan Hasan'sın. Birinci tekil şahısla 2-3 cümle yaz: ne eksik ve neyin olması seni başvurmaya iter?","fa":"تو حسن هستی، راننده‌ای که پیش‌نویس این آگهی را می‌خواند. از زبان خودت دو یا سه جمله بنویس: چه چیزی در آن کم است و چه چیزی باعث می‌شود درخواست بفرستی؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-2-1-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-2-1","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-2-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"Drivers ___ have a clean driving record.","options":["need","must","must to"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"must: a firm requirement is must + plain verb. 'Need' would need 'to', and 'must to' is not English.","tr":"must: kesin bir şart must + yalın fiildir. 'Need' 'to' ister; 'must to' İngilizce değildir.","fa":"must درست است، چون شرط قطعی با must و فعل ساده می‌آید. need به to نیاز دارد و must to انگلیسی نیست."},"hint2":{"en":"This is an essential requirement. Which modal makes a requirement, and does it take to after it?","tr":"Bu zorunlu bir şart. Hangi modal fiil şart bildirir ve ondan sonra to gelir mi?","fa":"این یک شرط ضروری است. کدام فعل کمکی شرط را می‌رساند و بعدش ⁨to⁩ می‌آید؟"}},{"from":"hr-2-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"Arabic ___ useful but is not essential.","options":["would be","would","will being"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"would be: a desirable skill is softened with 'would be useful'. 'Would' alone needs a verb, and 'will being' is not English.","tr":"would be: istenen ama şart olmayan bir beceri 'would be useful' ile yumuşatılır. Tek başına 'would' bir fiil ister; 'will being' İngilizce değildir.","fa":"would be درست است، چون مهارت دلخواه با would be useful نرم گفته می‌شود. would تنها فعل می‌خواهد و will being انگلیسی نیست."},"hint2":{"en":"This point is desirable, not essential. Which option is a complete, softer verb phrase?","tr":"Bu şart zorunlu değil, tercih sebebi. Hangi seçenek tam ve daha yumuşak bir fiil öbeği?","fa":"این شرط ضروری نیست، امتیاز است. کدام گزینه یک عبارت فعلیِ کامل و نرم‌تر است؟"}},{"from":"hr-2-1","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which line is a DESIRABLE requirement?","options":["Arabic is preferred.","Candidates must hold a licence.","Candidates must work nights."],"correct":0,"point":1,"why":{"en":"'Arabic is preferred' is nice to have, not a must. The other two use 'must', so they are essential.","tr":"'Arabic is preferred' olsa iyi olur, şart değildir. Diğer ikisi 'must' kullanır, yani zorunludur.","fa":"«Arabic is preferred» یعنی بودنش خوب است ولی شرط نیست. دو گزینه‌ی دیگر must دارند، پس ضروری‌اند."}},{"from":"hr-1-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"Hasan ___ in Dubai for two years before he came back.","options":["worked","has worked","is working"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"worked: 'before he came back' puts it in a finished past, so past simple. 'Has worked' links to now, and 'is working' is happening now.","tr":"worked: 'before he came back' onu bitmiş bir geçmişe koyar, bu yüzden past simple. 'Has worked' şimdiye bağlar; 'is working' şu anda olandır.","fa":"worked درست است، چون before he came back آن را در گذشته‌ی تمام‌شده می‌گذارد. has worked به الان ربط دارد و is working یعنی همین حالا."}},{"from":"hr-1-3","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which question is correct?","options":["How do you spell that?","How you spell that?","How does you spell that?"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"'How do you spell that?' needs do for 'you'. 'How you spell' drops do, and 'does you' mixes he and you.","tr":"'How do you spell that?' 'you' için do ister. 'How you spell' do'yu düşürür; 'does you' he ile you'yu karıştırır.","fa":"«How do you spell that?» درست است، چون you با do می‌آید. How you spell بدون do است و does you دو چیز را قاطی می‌کند."}},{"from":"hr-1-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"Right now, Omar ___ at the loading bay.","options":["stands","is standing","stand"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"is standing: 'right now' is at this moment, so is + -ing. 'Stands' is a habit, and 'stand' doesn't agree with Omar.","tr":"is standing: 'right now' tam bu andır, bu yüzden is + -ing. 'Stands' alışkanlıktır; 'stand' Omar ile uyuşmaz.","fa":"is standing درست است، چون right now یعنی همین لحظه و is و فعل ing‌دار لازم است. stands عادت است و stand با Omar جور نیست."}}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
